  <div class="about-page">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      <em>Bedroom Dialectics</em> is a notebook for thoughts that take too long to settle.
    </p>

    <p>
      Most things written here start late at night, when the day's noise dies down and an unaddressed observation stays stuck in the room. Writing them into sentences is simply a way to see if an idea holds weight once stripped of late-night melodrama.
    </p>

    <p>
      The essays jump between English and Bahasa Indonesia. Some look at physical infrastructure and historical footnotes; others pick at everyday habits, sports, or quiet corners of the city. There is no predetermined schedule or singular theme—just an attempt to look closely at ordinary things and write about them without pretense.
    </p>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>

    <p>
      Built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Astro</a>, rendered in static HTML and CSS, and set in <em>IBM Plex Mono</em>. No analytics, tracking scripts, popups, or cookies.
    </p>

    <p>
      Updates are published to the <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
